{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-post-template-tsx","path":"/posts/everything-is-interpretation/","result":{"data":{"markdownRemark":{"id":"7051edde-3b7e-5351-94f9-8c5699461da8","html":"<blockquote>\n<p>“Remember that all is opinion, and opinion is in thy power.”\n<em>Marcus Aurelius, Meditations 12.22</em></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 960px; \"\n    >\n      <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/198d82dc5b3025b19d7cbaf2cde1bdf7/5b6ee/image1.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n    <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 56.25%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <picture>\n          <source\n              srcset=\"/static/198d82dc5b3025b19d7cbaf2cde1bdf7/8ac56/image1.webp 240w,\n/static/198d82dc5b3025b19d7cbaf2cde1bdf7/d3be9/image1.webp 480w,\n/static/198d82dc5b3025b19d7cbaf2cde1bdf7/e46b2/image1.webp 960w,\n/static/198d82dc5b3025b19d7cbaf2cde1bdf7/f992d/image1.webp 1440w,\n/static/198d82dc5b3025b19d7cbaf2cde1bdf7/b47ac/image1.webp 1672w\"\n              sizes=\"(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px\"\n              type=\"image/webp\"\n            />\n          <source\n            srcset=\"/static/198d82dc5b3025b19d7cbaf2cde1bdf7/8ff5a/image1.png 240w,\n/static/198d82dc5b3025b19d7cbaf2cde1bdf7/e85cb/image1.png 480w,\n/static/198d82dc5b3025b19d7cbaf2cde1bdf7/d9199/image1.png 960w,\n/static/198d82dc5b3025b19d7cbaf2cde1bdf7/07a9c/image1.png 1440w,\n/static/198d82dc5b3025b19d7cbaf2cde1bdf7/5b6ee/image1.png 1672w\"\n            sizes=\"(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px\"\n            type=\"image/png\"\n          />\n          <img\n            class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n            src=\"/static/198d82dc5b3025b19d7cbaf2cde1bdf7/d9199/image1.png\"\n            alt=\"A runner standing still on a wet seaside road before dawn, arms open to the rain under a single streetlamp\"\n            title=\"\"\n            loading=\"lazy\"\n            decoding=\"async\"\n            style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n          />\n        </picture>\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<p>I usually run at around 5 a.m. Some mornings, it rains.</p>\n<p>When that happens, I have two options. I can let it put me in a bad mood, or I can accept it and continue with something else.</p>\n<p>I believe the impression is everything here. If I treat the rain as bad, the mood does not stay in that moment. It carries into the next hours, and sometimes into the next days.</p>\n<p>But I can also read it as a blessing. I can enjoy the rain, run in it anyway, or use the time for other tasks.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-event-doesnt-hurt-you-your-reading-does\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#the-event-doesnt-hurt-you-your-reading-does\" aria-label=\"the event doesnt hurt you your reading does permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>The event doesn’t hurt you, your reading does</h2>\n<p>Marcus Aurelius borrowed a line from a Cynic philosopher, that everything is interpretation. How I feel depends on how I read the rain.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>“Take away thy opinion, and then there is taken away the complaint, ‘I have been harmed.’ Take away the complaint, ‘I have been harmed,’ and the harm is taken away.”\n<em>Meditations 4.7</em></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>On a rainy morning, my first impression says “this is bad”. If I believe it without checking, the rest of my morning follows that reading.</p>\n<h2 id=\"your-readings-shape-who-you-become\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#your-readings-shape-who-you-become\" aria-label=\"your readings shape who you become permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>Your readings shape who you become</h2>\n<p>A single reading is small. The readings I repeat every day add up.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>“Such as are thy habitual thoughts, such also will be the character of thy mind; for the soul is dyed by the thoughts.”\n<em>Meditations 5.16</em></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>If I keep reading small things as bad, I become someone who is easily upset. If I keep accepting them and moving on, I become calmer. My mind takes the shape of the thoughts I let stay.</p>\n<h2 id=\"even-the-hard-things\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#even-the-hard-things\" aria-label=\"even the hard things permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>Even the hard things</h2>\n<p>I think this applies to grief, injustice, and physical pain too. They are harder to read well, but they are still interpretation.</p>\n<p>With proper tuning of the mind, I can see a hard situation clearly and then choose the necessary action, instead of reacting to my first impression of it.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-pause\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#the-pause\" aria-label=\"the pause permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>The pause</h2>\n<p>My practice is to pause before responding.</p>\n<p>When something happens, I remind myself that this is just an initial impression, and I don’t need to react automatically.</p>\n<p>That pause can be a couple of seconds or a few minutes. I use it to look at my emotion and at what is really happening, and then I decide on the proper action.</p>\n<p>It is a simple habit, but I find it very powerful.</p>\n<h2 id=\"to-my-sons\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#to-my-sons\" aria-label=\"to my sons permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>To my sons</h2>\n<p>You will have your own rainy mornings. Some will be actual rain, and some will be harder things.</p>\n<p>When something feels bad, pause first. Remind yourself that it is only your first impression. Then decide how to read it and what to do next.</p>\n<p>Be careful which thoughts you keep, because over time, your mind takes their shape.</p>","timeToRead":2,"fields":{"slug":"/posts/2026-10-24---everything-is-interpretation//posts/everything-is-interpretation","tagSlugs":["/tag/personal-development/","/tag/stoicism/","/tag/marcus-aurelius/","/tag/mindset/","/tag/life-tips/"]},"frontmatter":{"date":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["Personal Development","Stoicism","Marcus Aurelius","Mindset","Life Tips"],"title":"Everything Is Interpretation","description":"When it rains before my morning run, how I read it decides the rest of my day. A note for me, and for my sons.","socialImage":{"publicURL":"/static/198d82dc5b3025b19d7cbaf2cde1bdf7/image1.png"}}}},"pageContext":{"slug":"/posts/2026-10-24---everything-is-interpretation//posts/everything-is-interpretation"}},"staticQueryHashes":["4208939363"],"slicesMap":{}}